# zram swap table for the P22H190.
#
# The factory /vendor/etc/init/hw/init.ram.rc already carries the whole zram
# bring-up sequence, but its last step is
#
#     on property:sys.boot_completed=1
#         write /proc/sys/vm/swappiness 150
#         write /proc/sys/vm/page-cluster  0
#         write /sys/block/zram0/max_comp_streams 7
#         write /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm   lz4
#         swapon_all /vendor/etc/fstab.enableswap
#
# and the factory vendor image never shipped that file, so swapon_all had
# nothing to do and the device booted without any swap.  Install this table so
# the factory hook can run as designed.
#
# fs_mgr applies zramsize to the zram device (before mkswap) and then runs
# mkswap and swapon for every entry of type "swap", so this single line is
# equivalent to the previous hand-rolled
# "write disksize; mkswap; swapon -p 32758" setup.
#
# 6 GB DRAM -> 2 GiB zram.  max_comp_streams mirrors the value the factory rc
# writes, and swapprio is kept identical to the verified manual setup.
#
# Format: <device> <mount point> <type> <mount flags> <fs_mgr flags>
/dev/block/zram0    none    swap    defaults    zramsize=2147483648,max_comp_streams=7,swapprio=32758
